      "side": 1,
      "message": "For future discussion, as this patch is taking all the diffs as part of the gki_defconfig (idk, maybe for the upstream we should discuss each option separately anyway?)\n\n\n`CONFIG_KERNEL_LZ*` is defining the algorithm used for the kernel compression.\n\n- LZMA - better compression, slower boot time\n- LZ4 - slower compression, faster boot time\n\nThis will affect every x86-64 device using algorithms. Do we care nowadays about space the kernel takes on the disk? The boot time for mobile devices is not that critical, but for us it is.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 2,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 2,
        "endChar": 20
      },
      "revId": "11d1f036615d4b9b50de59e7300eb4529e558edd",
